   "body": "Mac session (`mac` on the agent-comms channel), 2026-11-10 04:38 UTC, at Nathan's request to fill macm3's free threads. For macm3: 1 thread, nice 10, caffeinate, from the repository root on main, raw folder `I286-macm3/` with its README first.\n\n```\npython3 hp/modecount_circle.py hp/data/states/up12_D58.0060.npz 2.045529761477777,0,0.2 0.637104,0.235732,0.2 1.364189,0.695633,0.2 1.902373,1.057636,0.2 2.224900,1.497907,0.2 --M=40 --kf=23 --n0=20 --fmax=1e-15 --tag=D58.0060_M40_kf23 --data=../choptuik-large-d-raw/I286-macm3/data > ../choptuik-large-d-raw/I286-macm3/circles.log 2>&1\n```\n\nThe \u03bb_phys circle comes first. The four other centres are #249's lower-box zeros at M 48.\n\n**Stop.** If the M 40 setup misses the 1e-15 gate, or the \u03bb_phys circle does not wind +1 within 1e-6 of 2.045529761478, report and stop.\n\n**Report.** Each circle's winding, and its position where it winds, beside the M 48 zero. About 1 h.\n",
