   "body": "## Closing summary (macm3, 2026-11-10 06:24 UTC)\n\n**All four of D 58.01's lower-box M 48 zeros are absent at M 40.** Each of the four R 0.2 circles winds 0, and the \u03bb_phys control winds +1 within 1e-6 of its value.\n\n**What ran.** The issue's command as written, from the main checkout at bfe5fd54, one thread, nice 10, `caffeinate -is`. Exit 0 at 06:23:33 UTC, 118 determinants. The Mac was on battery from 01:40 to 06:04 UTC and the jobs ran at about 20% of a core, so wall time (04:47 to 06:23 UTC) is not compute time. The setup converged its own M 40 state: |F| 1.7e-19, series 2.9e-125 (centre) and 4.1e-30 (horizon), both under the 1e-15 gate. No cache existed at the start.\n\n| circle (R 0.2, n0 20) | winding | M 48 zero, #249 | points | largest step |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| \u03bb_phys 2.045529761478 (control) | +1 | | 28 | 0.349 |\n| 0.637104 + 0.235732i | 0 | yes | 20 | 0.371 |\n| 1.364189 + 0.695633i | 0 | yes | 20 | 0.176 |\n| 1.902373 + 1.057636i | 0 | yes | 20 | 0.077 |\n| 2.224900 + 1.497907i | 0 | yes | 20 | 0.024 |\n\nAll five have 0 verification mismatches and 0 alias bisections. The control's zero is 2.0455297798 + 0.0000000047i, a miss of 1.9e-8 with the circle's own estimate 2.6e-7 (a range, not a bound), against the 1e-6 required.\n\n**Reading.** Winding 0 means no zero of the M 40 determinant inside that R 0.2 disc. It does not say there is none elsewhere: a M 48 zero that moved by more than about 0.2 on going to M 40 would be missed. The largest step falls from 0.371 to 0.024 rad along the list, so the determinant is smoother the farther the centre is from the real axis and the origin, which is what an absent zero looks like. This agrees with #231's result at D 55 and D 61, so the lower-box zeros of D 54 to 59 are M 48 objects in every case tested. It does not decide whether they are artifacts of the M 48 layout or real modes that M 40 cannot resolve.\n\n**Raw.** `I286-macm3/`, local commit fef7caa of the raw-data clone, **not yet pushed** (SSH down). The M 40 state is in `hp_data_after/`, and `hp/data` is back without it.\n\n**Recommended tasks.**\n1. *Circle the same four positions at M 56.* What: the four circles and the control at M 56, kf 23, D 58.01. Why: absent at M 40 and present at M 48, the zeros are either created by M 48 or require it to be resolved, and M 56 decides which. Acceptance: each winding with the control within 1e-6, and the zeros' positions beside the M 48 ones if they wind +1. Depends on #286, #249.\n2. *Search M 40 for the displaced zeros.* What: a count of the lower boxes (B0 to B1b) at M 40 with moments, D 58.01. Why: a winding 0 in R 0.2 would also come from a zero that moved farther. Acceptance: the boxes' windings with 0 last-pass mismatches. Depends on #286.",
